[{"id":"x70585","kind":"word","ko":"쓰다","yo":"","en":"to use (a tool, money, time)","pos":"동사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq70585_1","ko":"저는 휴대폰을 많이 써요.","en":"I use my phone a lot.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""}],"pron":"쓰다","roman":"","explain":"","video_url":"","video_title":"","phrases":[],"pron_source":"T111c DB v2.5.32 [미검증]","pron_why":null,"dict_examples":[],"explain_en":"","contract_en":"","dis":"","t153":"","t111c":true,"t90":""},{"id":"x50586","kind":"word","ko":"쓰다","yo":"써요","en":"to wear (hat, glasses)","pos":"동사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq50586_1","ko":"밖이 추우니까 모자를 써요.","en":"It's cold outside, so I wear a hat.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"써요","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50586_2","ko":"눈이 나빠서 안경을 쓰고 다녀요.","en":"My eyesight is bad, so I go around wearing glasses.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓰고","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50586_3","ko":"마스크를 쓰면 숨쉬기가 조금 힘들어요.","en":"It's a little hard to breathe when I wear a mask.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓰면","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50586_4","ko":"오늘은 햇빛이 강하니까 선글라스를 쓰세요.","en":"The sun is strong today, so wear sunglasses.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓰세요","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50586_5","ko":"자전거를 탈 때는 헬멧을 꼭 써야 해요.","en":"You must wear a helmet when riding a bike.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"써야","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50586_6","ko":"어제 제가 쓴 모자 못 봤어요?","en":"Did you see the hat I wore yesterday?","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓴","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""}],"pron":"쓰다","roman":"sseuda","explain":"모자, 안경, 마스크, 선글라스처럼 머리나 얼굴에 올리는 것에 써요. 옷은 '입다', 신발은 '신다', 시계는 '차다', 반지는 '끼다'를 써요. 우산을 쓰다(use an umbrella)도 같은 '쓰다'예요. 벗을 때는 '벗다'를 써요.","video_url":"","video_title":"","phrases":[{"ko":"안경을 쓰다","example":"저는 눈이 나빠서 안경을 써요.","en":"My eyesight is bad, so I wear glasses.","nuance_ko":"안경을 얼굴에 착용할 때 쓴다.","nuance_en":"Used for putting on or wearing glasses.","source":"AI [미검증]","en_equiv":"wear glasses"}],"pron_source":"앱 확장 [기본안]","pron_why":null,"dict_examples":[],"explain_en":"Use it for things you put on your head or face, such as hats, glasses, masks and sunglasses. Clothes use '입다', shoes use '신다', watches use '차다' and rings use '끼다'. Putting up an umbrella is also '쓰다', and taking things off is '벗다'.","contract_en":"","dis":"","t153":"","t111c":"","t90":{"pe":"v.","amb":1,"ax":"It's cold outside, so I wear a hat."}},{"id":"x50585","kind":"word","ko":"쓰다","yo":"써요","en":"to be bitter","pos":"형용사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq50585_1","ko":"커피가 너무 써요. 설탕 있어요?","en":"This coffee is too bitter. Do you have sugar?","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"써요","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50585_2","ko":"이 약은 입에 쓰지만 꼭 먹어야 해요.","en":"This medicine tastes bitter, but you must take it.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓰지만","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50585_3","ko":"설탕을 안 넣으면 맛이 써요.","en":"If you don't add sugar, it tastes bitter.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"써요","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50585_4","ko":"너무 쓰면 우유를 조금 넣어 보세요.","en":"If it's too bitter, try adding a little milk.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓰면","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50585_5","ko":"입이 써서 밥을 못 먹어요.","en":"My mouth tastes bitter, so I can't eat.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"써서","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""},{"id":"eq50585_6","ko":"이 채소는 맛이 좀 쓸 수 있어요.","en":"This vegetable can taste a bit bitter.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"쓸","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""}],"pron":"쓰다","roman":"sseuda","explain":"맛을 말하는 '쓰다'는 형용사라서 '써요, 써서'처럼 '아/어' 앞에서 '으'가 빠지고, 꾸밀 때는 '쓴 커피'가 돼요. 반대말은 '달다'예요. 글을 쓰다·모자를 쓰다는 동사라서 '쓰는 사람'처럼 '는'이 붙어요.","video_url":"","video_title":"","phrases":[{"ko":"쓴맛을 보다","example":"처음 사업에 실패하고 쓴맛을 봤어요.","en":"I got a bitter taste of failure when my first business failed.","nuance_ko":"실패나 어려움을 직접 겪고 힘들었다는 뜻이에요.","nuance_en":"It means going through failure or hardship yourself and finding it painful.","source":"AI [미검증]","en_equiv":"to get a taste of hardship"}],"pron_source":"앱 확장 [기본안]","pron_why":null,"dict_examples":[],"explain_en":"As a taste word it is an adjective. The '으' drops before '아/어', as in 써요 and 써서, and it becomes '쓴 커피' when modifying a noun. Its opposite is '달다' (sweet). The verbs for writing and wearing take '는', as in '쓰는 사람'.","contract_en":"","dis":"","t153":"","t111c":"","t90":{"pe":"adj."}},{"id":"x70586","kind":"word","ko":"내리다","yo":"","en":"to get off (a bus, train)","pos":"동사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq70586_1","ko":"저는 다음 정류장에서 버스에서 내려요.","en":"I get off the bus at the next stop.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""}],"pron":"내리다","roman":"","explain":"","video_url":"","video_title":"","phrases":[],"pron_source":"T111c DB v2.5.32 [미검증]","pron_why":null,"dict_examples":[],"explain_en":"","contract_en":"","dis":"","t153":"","t111c":true,"t90":""},{"id":"x70587","kind":"word","ko":"돌아가다","yo":"","en":"to spin, to turn around","pos":"동사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq70587_1","ko":"바퀴가 빙글빙글 돌아가요.","en":"The wheel spins round and round.","speech_level":"해요","cloze":"돌아가","extra_word":"","extra_grammar":"","tip":"","tip_en":""}],"pron":"돌아가다","roman":"","explain":"","video_url":"","video_title":"","phrases":[],"pron_source":"T111c DB v2.5.32 [미검증]","pron_why":null,"dict_examples":[],"explain_en":"","contract_en":"","dis":"","t153":"","t111c":true,"t90":""},{"id":"x70588","kind":"word","ko":"찍다","yo":"","en":"to stamp; to chop","pos":"동사","usage":"","contract":"","examples":[{"id":"eq70588_1","ko":"서류에 도장을 찍어요.","en":"I stamp the document with